  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When the sand is dropped on the conveyor belt its velocity will become equal to that of the conveyor. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>The force required to keep the conveyor belt moving will be equal to the gain in the momentum by the sand per second.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>v</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Now the power required to keep the conveyor belt moving will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
